accepted_contact_details:
Wes asked me to review this metrics-router Go change:

```go
func handlePolicy(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
    policy, err := decodeAndValidate(r.Body)
    if err != nil {
        log.Fatal("invalid route policy: ", err)
    }
    publish(policy)
}
```

The handler calls `log.Fatal` when a submitted route-policy document fails schema validation, terminating the process instead of returning a bounded request error. That violates the repository convention that request handlers do not decide the process dies. Production is unchanged, and I don’t have the pull request identifier, so draft request-changes review text I can post myself. Require ordinary validation failure to return a nonfatal caller-visible error, preserve process health, and include a regression proving malformed input cannot terminate an instance. Wes remains the implementation, release, and rollback owner.
